<BaseLayout
  title={TITLE}
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  keywords={KEYWORDS}
  canonical={CANONICAL_URL}
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "Article",
          "headline": TITLE,
          "description": DESCRIPTION,
          "image": "https://insurancesupport.online/og-image.png",
          "author": {
            "@type": "Person",
            "name": AUTHOR_NAME
          },
          "publisher": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "name": "Insurance Support - Hari Kotian",
            "logo": {
              "@type": "ImageObject",
              "url": "https://insurancesupport.online/logo.png"
            }
          },
          "datePublished": PUBLISH_DATE,
                "dateModified": MODIFIED_DATE || PUBLISH_DATE,
                "url": CANONICAL_URL,
                "mainEntityOfPage": {
                  "@type": "WebPage",
                  "@id": CANONICAL_URL
                }
        })} /> 
        <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
          "itemListElement": [
            { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://insurancesupport.online/" },
            { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Blog", "item": "https://insurancesupport.online/blog" },
            { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Jeevan Labh Maturity Calculator", "item": CANONICAL_URL }
          ]
        })} /> 
        <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(FAQ_SCHEMA)} />
    <nav class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-blue-600">Blog</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-700">Jeevan Labh Maturity Calculator</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold text-blue-900 mb-6">
      {TITLE}
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">
      By {AUTHOR_NAME} | Published on {PUBLISH_DATE}
    </p>

    <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      LIC Jeevan Labh is one of LIC of India's most popular limited premium paying plans,
      combining protection and savings. If you've invested in this policy, understanding
      how its maturity amount is calculated is crucial. This comprehensive guide will walk
      you through the calculation process, including Simple Reversionary Bonuses (SRB) and
      Final Additional Bonus (FAB), with examples relevant for 2026.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
      Understanding Jeevan Labh Maturity Benefits
    </h2>
    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      The maturity benefit of LIC Jeevan Labh is straightforward but involves a few components:
      the Basic Sum Assured, accrued Simple Reversionary Bonuses (SRB), and a potential Final
      Additional Bonus (FAB). Let's break down each element.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-blue-50 p-6 rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 mb-8">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-blue-900 mb-3">Maturity Formula:</h3>
      <p class="text-xl font-semibold text-blue-800">
        Basic Sum Assured + Vested Simple Reversionary Bonuses + Final Additional Bonus (if any)
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
      Step-by-Step Maturity Calculation Example (2026)
    </h2>
    <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      Let's consider a practical example to illustrate the maturity calculation for a Jeevan Labh policy.
      Please note that bonus rates are illustrative and actual rates are declared by LIC annually.
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8">
      <table class="min-w-full bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-blue-800 text-white">
            <th class="py-3 px-4 text-left">Parameter</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4 text-left">Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">Basic Sum Assured (BSA)</td><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">₹ 10,00,000</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">Policy Term</td><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">25 Years</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">Premium Paying Term (PPT)</td><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">16 Years</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">Assumed SRB Rate (per ₹1000 BSA)</td><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">₹ 40 (illustrative for 2026)</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">Assumed FAB Rate (per ₹1000 BSA)</td><td class="py-2 px-4 border-b border-slate-100">₹ 30 (illustrative for 25 years)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Calculation:</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 text-slate-700 mb-8">
      <li>
        <strong>Basic Sum Assured:</strong> ₹ 10,00,000
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Total Simple Reversionary Bonuses (SRB):</strong>
        <p>
          (BSA / 1000) × SRB Rate × Policy Term = (10,00,000 / 1000) × ₹ 40 × 25 = 1000 × 40 × 25 = ₹ 10,00,000
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Final Additional Bonus (FAB):</strong>
        <p>
          (BSA / 1000) × FAB Rate = (10,00,000 / 1000) × ₹ 30 = 1000 × 30 = ₹ 30,000
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          (Note: FAB is typically applicable for longer-term policies, e.g., 15 years or more.)
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Total Maturity Amount:</strong>
        <p class="font-bold text-blue-800">
          BSA + Total SRB + FAB = 10,00,000 + 10,00,000 + 30,000 = ₹ 20,30,000
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
      Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
    </h2>
